Subject: [PATCH] wmediumd: avoid success ACK amplification on hwsim transport

nl_send_auto_complete requests a kernel success ACK for every cloned RX frame
and TX status. A large multicast fanout therefore feeds administrative ACKs
back into the same receive socket carrying radio TX work. Disable automatic
success ACK requests after the synchronous generic-netlink family lookup.

Keep request flags, automatic sequence assignment, negative kernel replies,
and all radio delivery/802.11 ACK semantics unchanged. No buffer enlargement,
RF filtering, receive batching, or scheduler change is included.

--- a/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
+++ b/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
@@ -1882,6 +1882,8 @@ static int init_netlink(struct wmediumd *ctx)
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+	nl_socket_disable_auto_ack(sock);
+
 	nl_cb_set(ctx->cb, NL_CB_MSG_IN, NL_CB_CUSTOM, process_messages_cb, ctx);
 	nl_cb_err(ctx->cb, NL_CB_CUSTOM, nl_err_cb, ctx);
 
